---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Setup & Quick Start" currentPath="/docs/getting-started/quick-start">
  <div class="space-y-8 font-mono text-xs">
    <div>
      <div class="text-[11px] text-purple-400 font-semibold mb-1">GETTING STARTED</div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-sans">Setup & Quick Start Guide</h1>
      <p class="text-[#8f96a3] text-sm font-sans mt-1">Get RouteNex running locally in under 3 minutes with zero configuration.</p>
    </div>

    {/* Section 1 */}
    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#121622] border border-[#222738] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">1. Instant Launch with npx</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8f96a3] leading-relaxed">
        RouteNex runs completely standalone with no global dependencies. It automatically boots the local gateway on port 3001, loads free-tier provider pools, and launches Chrome or Edge straight into your authenticated dashboard:
      </p>
      <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-[#181d2c] border border-[#262f44] text-white">
        <code>npx routenex</code>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-[#7d8597]">
        Zero Cloud Login is required. RouteNex prints your local setup token in magenta and exchanges it for a local session automatically.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Section 2 */}
    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#121622] border border-[#222738] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">2. Test Your First Chat Completion</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8f96a3] leading-relaxed">
        Send an OpenAI-compatible request using curl, Python, or TypeScript. Notice you can pass <code class="text-purple-300">model: "auto"</code> to let RouteNex pick the fastest healthy free-tier provider:
      </p>
      <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-[#181d2c] border border-[#262f44] text-white overflow-x-auto">
        <pre><code>curl http://localhost:3001/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer rn-local-dev-default" \
  -d '&#123;
    "model": "auto",
    "messages": [
      &#123; "role": "user", "content": "Explain quantum teleportation in 2 sentences" &#125;
    ]
  &#125;'</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 3 */}
    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-[#121622] border border-[#222738] space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-sans">3. Connect Your Coding Agent CLI</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8f96a3] leading-relaxed">
        Use the built-in one-command launcher to launch Claude Code, Cursor, Cline, or Aider with isolated per-process environment variables:
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <div class="p-2 rounded bg-[#181d2c] border border-[#262f44] text-purple-300">
          <code>routenex run claude --model auto</code>
        </div>
        <div class="p-2 rounded bg-[#181d2c] border border-[#262f44] text-purple-300">
          <code>routenex run cursor</code>
        </div>
        <div class="p-2 rounded bg-[#181d2c] border border-[#262f44] text-purple-300">
          <code>routenex run aider --model combo/coding-power</code>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
